# Intended-exposure baseline — rig (CachyOS 192.168.10.12, AI stack + game servers)
# fix-51 (fleet-sweep SM56/SM58). Consumed by bin/listener-drift.sh.
#
# ALL-INTERFACE (0.0.0.0 / * / [::]) TCP LISTEN ports EXPECTED on rig and WHY.
# NOTE: the AI/GPU endpoints (ollama, llama-swap, comfyui, litellm, gpu-arbiter)
# publish on 0.0.0.0 and are UNAUTHENTICATED on the LAN — their only auth is at
# the mini Caddy edge, which a direct-LAN hit bypasses (fleet-sweep SM58,
# "Marinara-class hole"). Accepted on the trusted VLAN pending ha-19 IoT
# segmentation; captured here so a NEW listener (e.g. another debug nc) drifts.
# Host-IP / tailscale-IP / 127.0.0.1 binds (e.g. suwayomi 192.168.10.12:4567,
# palworld 127.0.0.1:25575) are intentionally NOT all-interface and out of scope.
#
# Format: one port per line; text after # is a comment.
22      # sshd (host)
1716    # kdeconnectd (host)
3000    # open-webui
3001    # lumiverse
3002    # marinara
4000    # litellm
5000    # local-deep-research (LDR, lai-08)
5355    # systemd-resolved — LLMNR (host)
8000    # mcpo
8080    # amp — CubeCoders AMP web
8188    # comfyui
8189    # gpu-arbiter
8199    # bioclip-api — BioCLIP 2 plant/species ID (lai-22)
8212    # palworld — REST admin API
8384    # syncthing — GUI
